# vba/vi_disp (id 422): block consumer of [OP, ARG] (inputs 65, 66). Classifies OP by 16
# thresholds and issues the first memory operation of the handler (table in interp.md):
# END -> vi_halt | JMP: IP = ARG, fetch ARG -> self | JZ, JNZ: read 2 at SP-2 -> vi_jz |
# LOAD: read 2 at FP+2ARG -> vi_load | STORE: read 2 at SP-2 -> vi_store | POP: SP -= 2,
# IP += 2, fetch -> self | CALL: read 4 at PROCT+4ARG -> vi_call | RET: read 4 at FP-2 -> vi_ret |
# PRINT, MSGBOX: read 2 at SP-2 -> vi_out | FORCHK: read 6 at SP-6 -> vi_for | OBJ -> vi_obj |
# binary and unary: read 4 at SP-4 -> vi_bin | PUSH (64+TAG): write [OP-64, ARG] at SP, SP += 2,
# IP += 2 -> vi_fetch | anything else: ERR += 51 -> vi_halt. OP, ARG saved in words 47, 48.
# Output 66 words (payload 64, 65 for PUSH). Note: weights/vba/interp.md
